+    <string name="info_got_it">Got it</string>
+    <string name="info_owner_title">Device owner</string>
+    <string name="info_restrictions_what">System-level rules for the whole phone, like blocking factory reset or app installs.</string>
+    <string name="info_restrictions_does">Lets you switch on Android\'s built-in restrictions, which Déchaîner can enforce because it\'s the device owner.</string>
+    <string name="info_restrictions_how">Each switch is a real Android policy, so the phone itself refuses the action. No app can bypass it. Recommended ones are listed first.</string>
+    <string name="info_apps_what">Suspend any app with one switch.</string>
+    <string name="info_apps_does">A suspended app is greyed out and won\'t open, and its notifications are hidden until you turn it back on.</string>
+    <string name="info_apps_how">Android itself suspends the app, because Déchaîner is the device owner. Turning a suspension on is instant; turning it off asks for your recovery code. An app held by a running schedule or impulse lock stays suspended until that ends.</string>
+    <string name="info_config_what">Settings for Déchaîner itself and its protections.</string>
+    <string name="info_config_does">Private DNS, protections, impulse lock, recovery code, unlock delay, keyboard type and forced removal.</string>
+    <string name="info_config_how">Anything that weakens protection goes through your recovery code, and through the unlock delay if you\'ve set one. Forced removal is the escape hatch: it lifts everything after a 48-hour wait, without the code.</string>
+    <string name="info_schedules_what">Weekly block windows, plus Study mode.</string>
+    <string name="info_schedules_does">A schedule suspends chosen apps, system features and websites at set times every week. With \"allow only\" on, it flips around: only the apps you list work. Duplicate a schedule, or copy apps from another, so you don\'t pick them twice.</string>
+    <string name="info_schedules_how">An exact alarm wakes Déchaîner at each window\'s start and end. Nothing polls in the background, so it costs almost no battery. Automatic time is forced while schedules are on, so changing the clock can\'t skip a window. \"Lock while active\" makes a running window uneditable.</string>
+    <string name="info_impulse_what">A lock on Déchaîner itself, for moments when you want to undo your own rules.</string>
+    <string name="info_impulse_does">Adds a challenge (math or typing) before the app opens, plus a panic button that locks Déchaîner, and optionally chosen apps, for 15 minutes to 6 hours.</string>
+    <string name="info_impulse_how">The challenge runs after authentication, every time you open Déchaîner. Until the panic timer runs out, Déchaîner stays locked.</string>
+    <string name="info_owner_what">The permission that makes blocking real.</string>
+    <string name="info_owner_does">Makes Déchaîner the device owner, which lets it suspend apps, apply system restrictions, and stop itself from being uninstalled.</string>
+    <string name="info_owner_how">Granted once via ADB or Shizuku during setup. Android only allows one device owner at a time.</string>
